robbery-390-392.l4:1079:1-48:
  TRUE
robbery-390-392.l4:1080:1-60:
  "You, Chen Weixiong Jerriek, are charged that you, on or about the 5th day of July 2002, at about 1.00pm, at void deck of Blk 121, Lor 1 Toa Payoh, Singapore, together with Koh Bang Long and Chia Jia Ting Samuel and in furtherance of the common intention of you all, did rob one Ng Juin Chye Joel of a handphone valued at about $450/-, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 392 read with section 34 of the Penal Code 1871."
robbery-390-392.l4:1081:1-60:
  "You, Chen Weixiong Jerriek, are charged that you, on or about the 5th day of July 2002, at about 1.00pm, at void deck of Blk 121, Lor 1 Toa Payoh, Singapore, together with Koh Bang Long and Chia Jia Ting Samuel and in furtherance of the common intention of you all, were jointly concerned in committing robbery of a handphone valued at about $450/- from one Ng Juin Chye Joel and whilst committing the said robbery, voluntarily caused hurt to him, to wit, by slapping him and banging his head against the wall, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 394 read with section 34 of the Penal Code 1871."
robbery-390-392.l4:1082:1-79:
  "A charge under section 392 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of robbery (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: neither the aggravation that makes a theft robbery (section 390(2)) nor the one that makes an extortion robbery (section 390(3))."
robbery-390-392.l4:1083:1-70:
  "You, Ravi s/o Muthu, are charged that you, on or about the 9th day of August 2004, at about 4.45 pm, at the footpath along Old Upper Thomson Road, Singapore, did rob one Zulkifli bin Hassan of a purse, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 392 of the Penal Code 1871."
